    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CX5zJbetBxLxSqjzM3W2XK)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Base: `main`.\n- Touches only `sp-frame` (`.el` and its literate `.org`).\n- Independent of every open PR. The `*Messages*` / `C-x b` thread may touch `sp-tabs`; no overlap in files, but both affect what `consult-buffer` shows.\n- Branch is named `465-...` but this is PR #466 (465 was taken meanwhile; a cloud session cannot rename a branch).\n\n## What\n- Problem: after `make-frame`, `C-x b` in the new frame shows almost nothing.\n- Cause (checked in the installed `tabspaces.el`):\n  - `tabspaces--local-buffer-p` and `tabspaces--buffer-list` read the `buffer-list` and `buried-buffer-list` frame parameters.\n  - `sp-tabs` uses `tabspaces--local-buffer-p` for the \"Workspace Buffers\" consult source, and hides the full source.\n  - A new frame has empty frame parameters.\n- Fix: new global minor mode `sp-frame-share-buffers-mode` in `sp-frame`, on by default.\n  - On `after-make-frame-functions` it copies `buffer-list` and `buried-buffer-list` into the new frame.\n  - `before-make-frame-hook` remembers the previously selected frame as the source.\n- Option `sp-frame-share-buffers-scope`:\n  - `selected` (default): copy from the previously selected frame, so the same workspace.\n  - `all`: every live, non-hidden buffer.\n- Command `sp-frame-share-buffers-now` does the same for an existing frame.\n\n## Synthetic frames\n- Frames made by code (the `vulpea-ui-view` frame from #447 calls `make-frame`), `emacsclient` frames and AeroSpace-tiled frames all run the hooks, so they are treated like normal frames.\n- Skipped: child frames (`parent-frame` parameter, e.g. posframe) and any frame with the `sp-no-share-buffers` parameter.\n- Errors are caught and only print a message, so `make-frame` never fails because of this.\n\n## Not verified\n- Not run in Emacs: the container has no Emacs and no GUI. Parentheses balance was checked with a script; the `.org` blocks tangle to the same text as the `.el` (checked by script).\n- Not tried with tabspaces sessions, `emacsclient`, or AeroSpace.\n- Frames already open are not changed until you run `M-x sp-frame-share-buffers-now`.\n- Per-tab lists of the new frame's other tabs are not populated.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 465-share-buffer-list-between-frames; git checkout 465-share-buffer-list-between-frames`, restart Emacs; no errors in `*Messages*`.\n- [x] Open a few files, `M-x make-frame`, `C-x b` in the new frame: the same \"Workspace Buffers\" appear.\n- [ ] Open the vulpea-ui view (`sp-vulpea-ui-view-open`): in its frame `C-x b` lists the buffers too.\n- [x] `emacsclient -c` frame shows the buffers.\n- [x] A posframe popup (e.g. completion) still works and no error appears.\n- [ ] `M-: (set-frame-parameter nil 'sp-no-share-buffers t)` then a frame made from it stays empty-listed (escape hatch), if you want to check.\n- [ ] `(setopt sp-frame-share-buffers-scope 'all)`: a new frame lists all buffers.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-frame-share-buffers-mode` off: new frames are empty again.\n- [ ] An older frame: `M-x sp-frame-share-buffers-now` fills it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8xdhv6htPzxTPgb4a)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8xdhv6htPzxTPgb4a",
